Types of Web Workers
1. Dedicated Worker

Used by a single script or page.

const worker = new Worker("worker.js");

Most commonly used.

2. Shared Worker

Can be shared between multiple tabs or windows.

const worker = new SharedWorker("worker.js");

Useful for:

Shared state
Cross-tab communication
3. Service Worker

Runs in the background and handles network-related tasks.

Common uses:

Progressive Web Apps (PWA)
Offline support
Push notifications
Caching